    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog hinges on chasing efficiency against exploitable starters, headlined by **Tyler Freeman** (68.21) and **Lawrence Butler** (65.41). **Tyler Freeman** is our strongest play, bolstered by a significant +14% park factor and the premium #2 lineup slot. Similarly, **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a massive +13% dynamic platoon edge and a hitter-friendly environment against Jos\u00e9 Soriano, making him a must-start despite his lower position in the order. We are also leaning into **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.07), who gains substantial value from a favorable matchup against Connor Prielipp and the added security of the #2 spot in the order. While **Taylor Ward** (63.85) carries a high score, keep a close eye on his -9% platoon penalty; his elite #1 positioning and wind-assisted upside against Roki Sasaki keep him in the green, though he remains a slightly higher-variance play than his peers.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer today was bypassing **Drew Gilbert** (40.82) for our final bench spot. While **Drew Gilbert** remains a high-upside asset, his projected #8 spot in the lineup dragged down his daily efficiency score, causing him to fall behind the consistent output of **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Matt Chapman**. We are exercising extreme caution with **Gavin Sheets** (41.13); his start is marginal at best, as he faces the daunting task of squaring off against Jacob deGrom. The -19% penalty from deGrom\u2019s elite skill level is a major concern, and **Gavin Sheets** is on a short leash to preserve our game caps if the matchup turns south early. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Daulton Varsho** currently sidelined on the IL, our depth is being tested, and we are relying on these tactical platoon advantages to keep us competitive in our pursuit of stolen bases and batting average.",
